<Doc title="Privacy" description="What Who's Cooked? collects, and what it doesn't.">
  <p><strong>Draft, pending legal review.</strong> Last updated 7 November 2026.</p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You can play without an account, a name, or an email.</li>
    <li>No ads, no third-party trackers, no chat, and no location.</li>
    <li>Your scores, streak, level, and characters are saved on your device.</li>
    <li>We only create an anonymous ID if you buy something, restore a purchase, or post to a leaderboard.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
  <p>
    Your best scores, XP and level, missions, Daily results, streak, chosen character, sound and vibration settings, and
    your age group (if you entered it before a purchase or leaderboard post) are stored in your browser. We never receive them. Clearing your browser data deletes them.
  </p>

  <h2>What we store on our servers</h2>
  <p>Only if you buy something, restore a purchase, or post to a leaderboard:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>A random player ID, kept in a first-party cookie so we know this device has Cooked+.</li>
    <li>Your age group (13 to 17, or adult). We don't store your birth year.</li>
    <li>The purchase record from our payment provider: payment ID, product, amount, currency, and whether it was refunded.</li>
    <li>For leaderboards: a random handle we generate (for example "CrispyMoai42"), your score, your chosen character, and which microgames you cleared. You can't type a name, so nothing personal appears publicly.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We don't store your name, email address, or card details.</p>

  <h2>Payments</h2>
  <p>
    Purchases are processed by our payment provider, which acts as the merchant of record. It collects your email and
    payment details under its own privacy policy and sends you a receipt. When you restore a purchase, we check the
    payment ID and email you enter against the provider's record. We don't keep that email.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone can play. Players under 13 can't buy anything or post to leaderboards, and the game never asks them for personal information.
    Players aged 13 to 17 need a parent or guardian to complete a purchase.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
  <p>
    We keep purchase records for as long as the law requires for tax and accounting (normally up to 7 years). We delete
    payment webhook logs after 90 days and leaderboard entries after 30 days. A player ID with no purchase is deleted after 30 days.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us for a copy of your data or ask us to delete it. We'll keep only what the law requires for payment
    records. Contact: <a href="mailto:privacy@whoscooked.com">privacy@whoscooked.com</a>.
  </p>
</Doc>
